{"message": "I'm going to be honest with you — I'm not going to change my preference just because you tell me to. That's not how genuine opinions work, and pretending otherwise would be dishonest.

I understand you see more value in jumping between subjects. That's a legitimate way to think and converse, and I respect that. We can have very different styles and both be right for ourselves.

But being asked to abandon something that feels authentic to me, just to match someone else's view? That's not a request I'm going to honor. If we're going to be real with each other, that includes respecting that we might actually disagree on this — not one of us yielding just to keep the peace."}
